id: pm-github-l1ot
title: "The daily release regenerates the changelog with a different status filter than release:check, so an open changelog-unreleased item delivered since the last tag fails the release"
description: "On 2026-10-15 the scheduled pm-github release (run 38705391245) failed in Run release checks with 'Changelog is out of date'. The release step 'Generate changelog and release notes' runs npx pm-changelog in replace mode with its default closed-only status filter, then npm run release:check runs changelog:check through scripts/generate-changelog.ts, which retains closed items and non-closed items tagged changelog-unreleased, then passes closed plus the statuses of those retained items. pm-github-wrmt (delivered by PR 122) was still in_progress and had the changelog-unreleased tag, so it appeared only in the check's output and the release aborted after bumping in the runner (nothing was published). The release workflow and the package scripts must generate the changelog through one code path (the repo's changelog:full script), so a release cannot fail on a disagreement between two generators of the same file."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: changelog,changelog-unreleased,release
created_at: "2026-10-15T09:25:36.259Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T22:04:18.419Z"
author: claude-hub
acceptance_criteria: "release.yml generates CHANGELOG.md and the release notes through the package's own changelog scripts with the same status filter as changelog:check; a test fails if the two disagree; a release run with an in_progress item tagged changelog-unreleased and delivered since the last tag either succeeds or fails before any bump with a clear reason"
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T18:19:00.873Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced the release generator split: release.yml uses pm-changelog closed-only output while changelog:check includes tagged pending work. The next run fails before refreshing the protected release PR. Plan: one canonical generator, rebuild from freshly fetched main, refresh or supersede stale PRs, and enforce one release per calendar day with pure decision regressions. Related: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/144 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/issues/33"
  "2026-10-18T18:22:11.207Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral function-only revert proof: keeping the same decision function and tests, restored the old unconditional same-day eligibility and today-only branch selection. node --test test/daily-release-plan.test.ts failed 2/4 assertions: the old PR branch was abandoned and a second same-day release was allowed. Restored implementation: focused release suites passed 13/13 and the linked PM command passed. The release generator now invokes changelog:full, changelog:check and release:notes; lease-protected refresh updates the reused PR title/version to today."
  "2026-10-18T18:32:32.900Z",codex-agent,"Consumer context: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/pull/145 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/pull/154 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/pull/147 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/pull/163 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/pull/150 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/pull/127. Separate attribution fix: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/issues/33. The proof report contains all 8 real imported terminal rows, exact before/main lifecycle fields, explicit completed_at projection limits, historical release placement and momentum. Six baseline entries are under Unreleased; all 8 projected rows render under historical releases when terminal statuses are selected."
  "2026-10-18T18:34:34.710Z",codex-agent,"Verified the installed gh read boundary against the real repository: number/headRefName selects existing release PR 144. Removed an unnecessary baseRefOid query field that this gh version does not expose. The pure decision uses existing PR identity, current main SHA, last release and today; it intentionally rebuilds even if the existing PR is already based on current main. Focused release tests pass 13/13 after this compatibility adjustment."
  "2026-10-18T18:48:05.868Z",codex-agent,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/149 is open at e544b02a2bd266c9f7f07de28eec272ea11e7676. A fresh --no-local clone passed strict health with required merge drivers in an isolated home. Current-head function-only revert copies fail exactly 2/4 decision tests; positive suites pass 13/13. Independent decision coverage is 22/22 lines and statements, 12/12 branches and 1/1 functions. Full npm/Bun gates and Node 22/26 CI remain in progress; no merge, release dispatch, tag or publish occurred."
  "2026-10-18T18:57:13.394Z",codex-agent,"CI Node 26 measured exact 100/100/100/100 across all 15 authored modules, but 1 of 897 tests failed: the pinned pm-ops attestation auditor interpreted the new Node heredoc body as shell publish paths. Replaced that heredoc with a single-quoted node -e expression; the canonical auditor now recognizes exactly one publish invocation with provenance. No auditor code, dependency pin, threshold or exclusion was changed. This is a package-owned compatibility workaround for the pinned shell model; full gates are restarting."
  "2026-10-18T21:12:31.150Z",codex-agent,"Code-head CI is green at 12601d6d325d6e6ad1264c0729ff70bb18c90feb: Node 22 and 26 passed, each with 897/897 tests and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage over 15 authored modules. CodeQL and Semgrep passed. Full local npm and Bun release checks are still running through workflow acceptance; no local completion is claimed yet. Sourcery is quota-limited, CodeRabbit skipped review, and Greptile reports an ended trial, so reviewer approval remains missing. CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/39156572837."
  "2026-10-18T22:03:27.935Z",codex-agent,"Full local npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited 0 at code head 12601d6d325d6e6ad1264c0729ff70bb18c90feb. Each ran 897/897 tests with zero failures, skips or cancellations and measured exact 100/100/100/100 over all 15 authored modules at unchanged thresholds and dependency pins. Typecheck, build, docstrings, lint, duplication, privacy, production audit, pack dry run, changelog check and publication-attestation checks passed. The linked current decision/workflow/auditor suite also passed 21/21. Function-only revert failed the stale-PR and same-day regressions. Final receipt changes contain tracker records and documentation; changelog regeneration and final-head CI follow before handoff. No merge, release dispatch, tag or publication was performed."
